WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:25.000
I take over Kaiba's duel, and Noa's Spirit Monsters attack me one after another.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.060
If I let my guard down, I'll lose instantly.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:33.050
I used Cyber Jar to make a comeback, but Noa's Deck Master's ability stopped it.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:36.100
The difference in our life points keeps growing.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.730
But I knew I'd be at a disadvantage.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:41.970
I can't afford to lose this duel!

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:49.020
10000 Life Points vs 100!!

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.290
Yugi!

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:56.230
It's over, Yugi!

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.900
I activate my trap card!

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.170
I won.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.610
I totally won!

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:09.780
Yugi!

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.540
Yugi!

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.010
Yugi!

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.280
What's wrong, Noa?

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.840
I'm still alive.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.260
Impossible!  I pulverized Kuriboh!

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:27.400
Look at my field.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.800
A trap card!

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.620
That's right.  Nutrient Z!

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:42.540
When I take at least 2000 points of damage, I gain 4000 life points first.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:47.900
So even after taking damage, my life points increase to 1800.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.040
Too bad.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.680
Your prediction was wrong!

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:05.740
But by surviving, you will witness a horrifying reality.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:06.800
What?

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.530
I still dealt you damage during the battle.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:15.220
Therefore, my Deck Master's ability activates.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.740
I regain life points.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:21.400
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Sebek's Blessing.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.850
When my monster attacks you directly...

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:29.100
...I gain life points equal to the damage you took.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.200
Now return, Yamata Dragon!

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.660
Spring of Rebirth's effect activates!

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.070
How's that, Yugi?

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.520
11,000 life points?

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:49.510
How can he erase so many life points?

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.350
Kaiba, Mokuba, Otogi...

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:59.250
I vowed to carry on their bond.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.250
I can't afford to lose.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.190
My turn!  I draw!

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:09.130
I summon Alpha The Magnet Warrior in attack position!

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:11.430
Attack Noa directly!

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.430
Magnet Sword!

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:20.220
That weak attack doesn't hurt at all.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.210
I end my turn.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:24.860
My turn.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:30.380
But before that, Yugi, I'll further your countdown to despair!

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.620
Honda!

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:39.560
Honda!

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.290
Noa!  How dare you!

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:46.500
Every time it's my turn, you lose a friend.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.500
What you're doing is pointless!

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.940
We still believe in Yugi!

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.820
Don't worry.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:58.510
I'll let you watch your sister's demise.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:01.310
Brother...

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:02.900
Stop this, Noa!

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.750
Saving them is simple.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:08.380
Just defeat me.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:09.720
Easy, right?

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.190
Try it, Yugi!

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:14.360
Try it, Yugi!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.440
My turn.  I draw.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:23.330
I summon the Spirit Monster, Inaba White Rabbit.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:30.340
This card can attack you directly, even if you have monsters on your field.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:31.780
What?

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.380
Attack Yugi directly!

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.840
Return, White Rabbit!

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:54.570
Due to my Deck Master's ability and Spring of Rebirth, I gain life points again.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.830
Noa gained life points again.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.100
Brother...

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.840
It's fine, Shizuka.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.240
Yugi will win.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.810
My turn.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.610
I set a card.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:10.850
Then I tribute Alpha The Magnet Warrior.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.780
To summon Dark Magician Girl!

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:24.530
She gains 300 attack points for every Dark Magician in my graveyard.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:28.690
Go, Dark Magician Girl!

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.730
Attack Noa directly!

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:36.170
What's wrong, Yugi?

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:39.910
That's not good enough to save your friend's sister.

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:42.160
What'll you try next?

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.340
I... end my turn.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.260
Brother...

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:55.230
My turn!  Countdown to despair!

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.830
Brother!  Watch out!

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.800
Shizuka!

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:04.500
Shizuka!

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.500
Brother...

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:07.970
Shizuka!

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:15.140
Shizuka!

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:18.480
I'm sorry, Jonouchi.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.590
Yugi, revel in your helplessness.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.250
My turn.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:28.210
I summon the Spirit Monster, Inaba White Rabbit!

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:32.630
Noa, I was waiting for this moment.

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:37.200
I activate the trap card, Dark Renewal!

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:39.080
A trap?

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:45.010
Dark Renewal activates when you summon a monster.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:49.970
In exchange for the monster you summoned and one of my monsters...

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.950
...I can resurrect a Spellcaster from the graveyard.

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:54.780
So, Noa...

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.390
I tribute your Inaba White Rabbit!

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.050
What?

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:00.990
And my defending monster!

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:03.530
The monster I'll resurrect is...

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.720
Come out, Dark Magician!

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.340
What?

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:23.580
Since your Spirit Monster doesn't return to your hand, your life restoration combo doesn't activate!

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.720
I set a card and end my turn.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:31.720
Are you sure, Noa?

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:33.660
Your field is empty.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.660
Just wait, everyone.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.590
I'll restore you to normal.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:39.760
I draw!

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:47.000
Noa, I'll show you the true power of my deck!

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.140
I activate my spell card!

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.570
Black Magic Ritual!

00:08:56.710 --> 00:09:03.180
I tribute my Level 8 Valkyrion the Magna Warrior from my hand.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:09.630
My tribute fuels the ritual!

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:13.600
Appear from the chaos of darkness!

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.240
Magician of Black Chaos!

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:20.700
What?

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:36.520
Dark Magician, Dark Magician Girl and Magician of Black Chaos!

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:40.460
The Three Musketeers of black magic are here!

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:42.460
Three Magicians!

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.870
7300 total attack points!

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:47.400
He can turn the tables!

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.280
Go!  Three Musketeers of dark magic!

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.500
Attack Noa directly!

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.510
Take this!  Triple Black Magic!

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:23.030
Just kidding.  Not good enough.

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:27.900
I activate the trap card, Chaos Barrier Field!

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.080
What?

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:35.560
This trap card activates when your monster attacks.

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:43.690
Your strongest and weakest monsters must battle, and the Battle Phase ends.

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:46.620
My barrier will be...

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.620
Dark Magician Girl.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:53.120
Take Magician of Black Chaos's attack!

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.060
Magician Girl!

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:58.200
Your Battle Phase ends.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:04.120
And I regain life points equal to the damage you took.

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:07.550
Noa gained life points again.

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:10.900
You're impressive, Yugi.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:14.250
Your judgment and actions to strike at weaknesses.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:18.590
When you think about it, we don't need to be enemies.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:25.380
If you promise to help me, I'll free your friends.

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:26.450
What?

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:29.030
Except Seto and Mokuba.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:30.700
They'll be back to normal?

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:33.130
Shizuka.

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:36.140
Seto is your enemy.

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:40.610
So you shouldn't care what happens to Seto.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:43.540
Don't you want your friends back?

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:50.890
No, Yugi!

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:52.820
Jonouchi...

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.460
Jonouchi.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:57.970
Kaiba may be our enemy.

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:02.880
But he cares about his brother like how I care about my sister.

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:06.200
Otogi, Honda, even Shizuka would say the same thing!

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:07.900
Yugi, fight!

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:08.870
Please fight!

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:10.540
And win!

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:12.610
Jonouchi...

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:16.800
Nobody asked for your lame opinion, lame-o!

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.550
My turn!

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:23.680
Jonouchi!

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:26.740
Jonouchi!

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:31.290
Noa!  I feel sorry for you!

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:32.230
What?

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:36.100
Even though you're smarter, your heart is still immature.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.600
You hate what you don't have.

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:40.830
You're nothing but a selfish child!

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:46.000
Ordinary people can't understand my greatness.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.700
Victory only comes to the chosen ones.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.740
Yugi, I choose you.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:54.720
Say that you'll cooperate with me!

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:58.150
You use power to manipulate people.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:02.370
So no one will accept you!

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:04.090
You're a fool, Noa!

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:06.750
Did you call me a fool?

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:11.330
It's sad that you're such an idiot!

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:13.770
You'll get what you asked for!

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:14.300
I draw!

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:16.240
I set a monster in defense.

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:19.670
I also set another card.

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:26.350
Since you're close to death, I'll tell you what this card is.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:30.730
The card I'll set is Ground Breaking.

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:35.960
It lets me bring one Spirit Monster in my graveyard back to my hand.

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:39.390
I'll retrieve Inaba White Rabbit, of course.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:42.400
You only have 300 life points.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:47.330
Inaba White Rabbit has 700 attack points, so the duel will end when it attacks you.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:49.770
With my victory.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:53.210
I end my turn.

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:55.910
The battle isn't over yet!  I draw!

00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:01.680
I activate the trap card, Ground Breaking!

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:06.220
Inaba White Rabbit returns from the graveyard to my hand.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:07.750
I don't think so!

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:11.190
The spell card, Card Destruction!

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:17.600
After you discard your entire hand, draw the same number of cards from your deck.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:20.050
Magician of Black Chaos!

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:21.800
Attack the defending monster!

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:24.370
Chaos Magic!  Death Ultima!

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.100
I caught you!

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:29.350
Otohime's effect activates!

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:33.020
She switches your monster's battle position.

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:36.350
Dark Magician switches to defense position!

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:41.620
This ends Dark Magician's Battle Phase.

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:48.440
Since my Spirit Monster was destroyed, my trap card activates!  Vessel of Illusion!

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:51.730
I Special Summon a Token to tribute.

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:55.200
I summon Otohime again in defense position.

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.340
It's my turn, but...

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:02.510
Isn't it sad that no one will watch our duel anymore?

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:04.200
Anzu!

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:07.380
If you have any last words, let me hear it.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:11.420
I know!  How about something angry towards Yugi?

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:12.820
Whatever!

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:16.250
Yugi will win!

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:19.090
I always trust Yugi!

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:20.260
Anzu...

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:26.480
In that case, I'll get rid of you at the end of my turn.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.600
You'll probably change your mind by then.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:31.970
Just like this card.

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:34.970
The spell card, Change of Heart!

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:38.480
I gain control of one of your monsters until the end of the turn.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.410
I choose...

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:42.720
Dark Magician!

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:47.680
How does it feel when your deck's icon becomes your enemy?

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:51.160
I tribute Dark Magician and Otohime.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:57.530
I summon the Spirit Monster with the most attack points!  Hino-Kagu-Tsuchi!

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:08.340
And a Spirit Equip Spell!

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:09.940
Flaming Fist!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:14.280
It adds 200 attack points for one turn.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.460
Go!  Hino-Kagu-Tsuchi!

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:18.130
Crimson Annihilation Fist!

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:34.060
Due to my Deck Master's ability and Flaming Fist, I regain 700 life points.

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:38.660
I activate the Continuous Spell, Spiritual Energy Settle Machine.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:41.080
I discard one card from my hand.

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:47.210
This card allows Spirit Monsters to stay on the field even after the turn is over.

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:51.480
I have exactly a hundred times as many life points than you.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.420
And you think you can make a comeback?

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:58.160
Yugi, please stand up!

00:16:58.500 --> 00:16:59.590
Fool.

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:00.580
Vanish!

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:03.820
Yugi...

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:07.680
Anzu!

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:11.740
Everyone is now gone.

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:17.180
Yugi, this really will be your last turn.

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:22.130
He has Hino-Kagu-Tsuchi with 2800 attack points.

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:24.600
But I have no monsters on my field.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:27.130
And zero cards in my hand.

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:28.700
It's impossible.

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:30.860
Am I going to lose?

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:33.650
I no longer have any friends who believe in me-

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.200
Partner!

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:39.250
My other self, I'm still here.

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:43.440
And not just me.  C'mon.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:49.360
This is the room in my heart.

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:54.800
My other self, we haven't found the room containing your memories yet.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.720
But there's a new room in here.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.050
A new room?

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:00.300
Yes.

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:05.000
This is the new room?

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:05.430
Yeah.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.260
Jonouchi!

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:09.800
Anzu!

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:13.820
Honda!  Otogi!  Shizuka!

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.230
I see!  This room is...

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:20.210
This memory room was created when you met us.

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:21.170
Yugi!

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:24.280
No one has left your side.

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:27.340
That's right.  We're always with you.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:29.450
And cheering for you.

00:18:30.550 --> 00:18:34.870
But there's no way I can win.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:35.750
Yugi.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:39.420
I've accepted you as my eternal rival.

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:41.730
Kaiba.  Mokuba.

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:45.920
You're going to stay here and whine?

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:46.670
Kaiba...

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:50.060
Our souls have combined into that deck.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:52.440
So it's the strongest deck there is.

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:56.580
The deck still has a chance to win.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:19:00.480
The deck has a chance to make a comeback...

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.280
Fight, Yugi.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:04.250
Believe in our deck.

00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:11.260
We still have a chance.

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:14.460
You're going to keep fighting?

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:17.930
Noa!  I still have things to protect!

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:19.450
I draw a card!

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:21.800
Card of Sanctity!

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:27.500
We both draw until we have six cards in our hands.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.020
Yugi.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:38.860
Take this, Yugi.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:40.570
We entrust you...

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:41.750
...with our hopes.

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:43.620
Here, Yugi.

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:44.660
Counting on you.

00:19:45.940 --> 00:19:48.440
These cards contain their hopes.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:55.100
Noa, let me tell you my first and last prediction for this duel.

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:58.100
You won't take another turn!

00:19:58.100 --> 00:20:00.590
The spell card, Monster Reborn!

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:02.540
The resurrecting monster is...

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:05.520
Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:08.580
Blue-Eyes!

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:11.250
Noa!  Me and Mokuba's anger will strike you!

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:15.140
Kaiba, your fight wasn't meaningless!

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:18.200
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:22.910
Next is the spell card, Polymerization!

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:29.530
I fuse two Blue-Eyes in my hand with the Blue-Eyes on my field!

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.140
What?

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:33.370
Come out!

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:35.910
The strongest servant in Kaiba's Deck!

00:20:39.770 --> 00:20:42.110
Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon!

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:43.780
And another spell card!

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:47.520
I use Quick Attack and attack Hino-Kagu-Tsuchi!

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:49.920
Ultimate Burst!

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:57.830
I'm far from defeated!

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:02.840
Noa, I told you that you won't get another turn.

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.000
De-Fusion!

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:11.110
Due to De-Fusion, the three Blue-Eyes can still conduct their Battle Phase.

00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:14.550
No way...  Can I do anything?

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:18.260
Noa!  The anger for toying with our bond!

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:21.140
And Kaiba and Mokuba's sorrow!

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:23.940
I'll end them both with this single strike!

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:26.360
Go, Blue-Eyes!

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:30.740
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:37.480
No way!  Is this the strength of their bond?

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:49.040
Hooray!  Yugi won!

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:51.660
Everyone's back to normal!

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:55.260
Huh?  Honda, why are you still a monkey?

00:21:55.260 --> 00:22:01.720
Noa!  Give Honda his body back and free us from this virtual world!

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:04.580
What?  No one can escape?

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:08.070
Noa, you don't control this world?

00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:10.420
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Kaiba Family's Darkness

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:11.860
Duel, standby!

00:22:16.090 --> 00:22:23.990
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:23.990 --> 00:22:32.940
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:33.270 --> 00:22:37.910
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:37.910 --> 00:22:41.880
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:42.310 --> 00:22:49.850
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:49.850 --> 00:22:53.420
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:53.420 --> 00:22:58.190
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:58.190 --> 00:23:08.300
And walk it without stopping

00:23:08.300 --> 00:23:15.910
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:24.880
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:32.860
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:42.700
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
